# The shared core: the files every chat loads or every machine runs (SU-Q89), and .github/ (SU-Q106).
# A change to any of them waits for a yes from every owner named on its line, other than its author.
#
# Adding an owner: only someone with write access to the repo (a line naming someone without
# write access is invalid and GitHub skips it). Add their @login to the end of every line below, so each
# line names everyone, for example:  /tools/ @iantutunaru @second-owner
#
# These lines are also what the core-approvals check reads (tools/core_approvals.py,
# .github/workflows/core-approvals.yml). It understands only the forms used here: a path from the repo's
# root starting with "/", a "*" inside a name, a trailing "/" for a folder, and @login owners. Any other
# form turns the check red and names the line.

/global/rules*.md @iantutunaru
/profiles/ @iantutunaru
/global/settings.json @iantutunaru
/global/hooks/ @iantutunaru
/install.ps1 @iantutunaru
/install-chatgpt.ps1 @iantutunaru
/tools/ @iantutunaru
/.github/ @iantutunaru
